<div class="bt-list"><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1">Categories</a> &gt; <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1019">sciences</a> &gt; <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=291">earth sciences</a> &gt; <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=464">geology</a></div>
<div class="row">
<div class="this-term col-sm-12">
  <div class="pref-label">economic geology</div>
  <div class="scope-note">Scientific study of the formation, location, and use of marketable geologic materials including fuels, metals, minerals, and water.</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="row mb-4">
<div class="col-sm-12">
  <div class="col-sm-8"><b>Subtopics</b><br/><span class="text-muted">(none)</span></div>
  <div class="col-sm-4"><b>See also</b><br/><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=132" title="Deposits of rocks used in construction, including crushed stone and dimension stone. Dimension stone includes limestone and granite, quarried in large blocks, and shaped in cubes, panels and other forms.">building stone resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=164" title="Fine-grained sedimentary soil deposits, containing hydrated silicas of aluminum, that are plastic and sticky when wet and harden when heated.">clay deposits</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=172" title="Fuel resources such as anthracite, lignite, bituminous coal, or coke, consisting largely of carbonaceous material and formed from fossilized plants.">coal resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=173" title="Resources of methane-rich gas generated and stored in coalbeds.">coalbed methane resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=799" title="Natural resources that are used for heat and power generation, including oil, natural gas, coal, and geothermal energy.">energy resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=427" title="Deposits of a crystalline solid in which water molecules trap gas molecules, usually methane, in a cagelike structure known as a clathrate occurring in sediments overlain by cold deep water.">gas hydrate resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=429" title="Deposits of rare minerals prized for their color, durability, sparkle, and clarity when cut and polished and used as ornaments or jewelry.">gem resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=500" title="Alluvial accumulations of small unconsolidated rock fragments, such as pebbles and cobbles, used in construction as fill, ground cover, or aggregate for concrete.">gravel deposits</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=2295" title="Interactions among groundwater, hydrocarbons, and rock properties of subsurface geological formations, affecting the potential of those formations to form, trap, and permit the passage and extraction of hydrocarbons.">hydrocarbon reservoir processes</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=724" title="Resources from which ductile, malleable, opaque,and reflective metals that are also good heat and electricity conductors can be extracted.">metallic mineral resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=745" title="Natural occurrences of useful inorganic elements or compounds.">mineral resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=770" title="Stocks of naturally formed hydrocarbon gases which are usually associated with petroleum fields.  Useful for heating, they are principally methane, but can be ethane, butane, or propane.">natural gas resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=798" title="Useful mineral deposits that are not metals.  Includes materials used for construction, decoration, fuel, and industrial purposes.">nonmetallic mineral resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=829" title="Deposits (pools) of highly valuable liquid hydrocarbons or fossil fuels.">oil resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=830" title="Deposits of sandstone or unconsolidated sand containing bitumen that can be extracted as an oil resource.">oil sand resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=831" title="Deposits of finely grained sedimentary rock containing kerogen that can be distilled to produce liquid or gaseous hydrocarbons.">oil shale resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1011" title="Deposits of loose particles of rock or mineral (sediment) that range in size from 0.0625-2.0 millimeters in diameter.">sand deposits</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1080" title="Natural resources of unconsolidated fragmented rock, humus, and mineral matter that cover the surface of the earth.">soil resources</a><br/>
</div>
